## WHAT AIANA IS

AIANA is the semantic memory system for the entire fabric. It:
  1. Captures conversations from Claude Code sessions via file watcher or hooks
  2. Stores them across four backends optimized for different retrieval patterns
  3. Exposes memory tools via an MCP server on port 8765
  4. Serves as the L5 (Session/Memory) layer in the fabric-sdk OSI model
  5. Acts as a reusable memory primitive — deployable standalone, as a sidecar,
     or as a per-fabric isolated instance

AIANA's design philosophy: flexible deployment. It can be:
  - Central shared memory across all fabrics (current deployment)
  - Per-fabric isolated instances (each fabric gets its own AIANA + Qdrant)
  - Embedded as a sidecar alongside any fabric container
  The deployment pattern emerges from operational need, not upfront design.

Project repository: ry-ops/aiana (Python)
Language: Python (pip installable, also Docker Compose)
Status: Production — 229+ messages recorded, Mem0 integrated, MCP server live

