## STORAGE ARCHITECTURE — FOUR BACKENDS

AIANA stores memories across four backends, each optimized for a different
retrieval pattern:

### 1. SQLite — Full-Text Search
  Purpose: Fast keyword search, structured queries, session indexing
  Location: ~/.aiana/memory.db (or configured path)
  Schema (messages table):
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY
    session_id TEXT
    project TEXT
    role TEXT ('user' | 'assistant')
    content TEXT
    timestamp DATETIME
    metadata TEXT (JSON blob)
  Current state: 229+ messages, ~660KB database
  FTS5 virtual table enables full-text search over content field
  ⚠ Known issue: SQLite binding errors on cortex-platform transcripts
    Error: "binding parameter 5: type 'list' is not supported"
    Cause: JSONL transcript format has list-type fields in metadata
    Fix needed: serialize list fields to JSON string before binding

### 2. Redis — Session Cache & User Preferences
  Purpose: Fast in-session context, user preferences, ephemeral state
  Current state: 1.07MB memory, caching enabled
  Key patterns:
    aiana:session:{session_id}     — session metadata (TTL: 24h)
    aiana:pref:{user}:{key}        — user preferences (persistent)
    aiana:cache:{hash}             — embedding cache (TTL: configurable)
  User preference commands: aiana prefer <key> <value>
  Preferences: persistent (survives restarts) or temporary (session-scoped)
  Auto-bootstrap: preferences are loaded into context at session start

### 3. Qdrant — Vector Semantic Search
  Purpose: Semantic similarity search, "find things related to X"
  Collection: aiana_memories (configurable)
  Vector dimensions: depends on embedding model (typically 1536 for OpenAI,
    768 for sentence-transformers, model-specific for Voyage AI)
  Current state: HEALTHY but 0 vectors indexed
  ⚠ Known critical issue: Vector indexing pipeline not producing vectors
    229 messages in SQLite, 0 in Qdrant
    Embedding step failing silently or not running
    This is the highest priority fix — semantic search is non-functional until resolved
  Payload schema per vector:
    {
      "message_id": "...",
      "session_id": "...",
      "project": "...",
      "role": "user|assistant",
      "content": "...",
      "timestamp": "...",
      "tags": []
    }

### 4. Mem0 — AI-Native Semantic Memory
  Purpose: Conversational memory with automatic extraction and deduplication
  Added: recently (post-February 2026 based on session history)
  Status: Integrated and operational ("100% operational with mem0 just added")
  What Mem0 adds over raw Qdrant:
    - Automatic memory extraction from conversations (no explicit save needed)
    - Deduplication: merges similar memories rather than storing duplicates
    - User/session scoping: memories are associated with context identities
    - Temporal decay: older memories can be weighted lower
    - Contradiction resolution: if new info contradicts stored memory, updates it
  Mem0 sits as a layer ABOVE Qdrant — it manages Qdrant as its vector store
  AIANA configuration: Mem0 connects to aiana-qdrant, not a separate instance

