## DATA INGESTION PIPELINE

### File Watcher Mode (Active, Current Method)
  Monitors: ~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session-id>.jsonl
  Trigger: inotify/polling on JSONL file changes
  Process:
    1. Detect new/modified .jsonl file
    2. Parse JSONL → extract role + content per line
    3. Filter: skip tool_use and tool_result blocks (content only)
    4. Write to SQLite (messages table)
    5. Queue for embedding → write to Qdrant ← THIS STEP IS BROKEN
    6. Feed to Mem0 for memory extraction
  Console output: "Recorded: user" / "Recorded: assistant" (confirms SQLite write)
  Limitation: passive monitoring, no real-time session awareness

### Claude Hooks Mode (Target State, Not Yet Configured)
  Hook events available in Claude Code:
    SessionStart    — inject AIANA context at session begin
    PostToolUse     — capture tool results in real-time
    SessionEnd      — finalize and summarize session
  Configuration location: ~/.claude/settings.json
  Current state: NO hooks configured — file watching only
  Impact:
    ✅ Can capture sessions via file monitoring
    ❌ Cannot inject context at SessionStart
    ❌ Cannot capture PostToolUse events in real-time
    ❌ No session lifecycle awareness
  Hook configuration template:
    {
      "hooks": {
        "SessionStart": "aiana hook session-start --session $SESSION_ID",
        "PostToolUse": "aiana hook tool-use --tool $TOOL_NAME",
        "SessionEnd": "aiana hook session-end --session $SESSION_ID"
