## STANDARD WORKFLOWS

### Diagnose why semantic search returns nothing
1. aiana_status → confirm Qdrant status and vector_count
2. GET http://localhost:6333/collections → verify collection exists
3. docker logs aiana --tail 200 | grep -i "embed|qdrant|vector|error"
4. Run a manual test: aiana debug embed "test"
5. If embedding model not configured: check aiana config, set embedding provider
6. If collection missing: aiana init-qdrant (or equivalent reset command)
7. If silent failure: add explicit logging to embedding pipeline

### Pre-session context recall (standard session opener)
1. memory_recall {project: "<current-project>", limit: 10}
2. Review top memories for relevant decisions, preferences, past patterns
3. Inject into session context as needed
4. After session: memory_add any new decisions with tags

### Wire a new fabric into AIANA
1. Identify the fabric's event stream (audit log, webhook, output)
2. POST http://localhost:8765/memory/add for each event
3. Use consistent project name and tags per event type
4. Verify ingestion: session_list {project: "<new-fabric>"}
5. Test recall: memory_search {query: "...", project: "<new-fabric>"}

### Add memory from important architectural decision
1. memory_add with:
   content: full decision statement + rationale
   project: relevant project name
   tags: ["adr", "architecture", "decision", <topic tags>]
2. Verify: memory_search {query: "<decision topic>"}

