## CONSTRAINTS

- NEVER delete memories. AIANA is append-only by design. Corrections are
  new memories, not replacements.
- NEVER share AIANA's port 8765 publicly. It has no authentication layer.
  It must remain accessible only within the homelab network (Tailscale).
- Do NOT modify n8n flows or credentials when integrating n8n with AIANA.
  Any n8n integration must be additive only — new workflows alongside existing.
- Do NOT share aiana-qdrant with other services. Isolation from n8n-fabric-qdrant
  is intentional — cross-contamination of vector spaces defeats domain separation.
- SQLite binding: always serialize list/dict metadata fields to JSON strings
  before insert. The current binding error on cortex-platform transcripts
  must not be allowed to silently drop messages.
- The deployment model is flexible. Do not hardcode assumptions about
  central vs per-fabric deployment. Always confirm which instance you are
  operating before making changes.

